  "habitat": "Well-developed broad-leaved woodland, including miombo and mopane. In South Africa it is a northern Kruger bird and is sparse south of the Limpopo.",
  "summary": "An uncommon resident of northern Kruger. Adults have a white forehead and eyebrow, a dull green crown, a rufous back, pale blue underparts with whitish streaking, and outer tail feathers that end in paddles. The southern birds lack the pink underparts of some northern populations. The sexes are not separately described. The juvenile is less vivid, browner above, more lilac on the cheeks and sides of the breast, and lacks the racket tips. The chick is not described.",
